        "original_id": "7fb7812e-bf08-5d21-8ffc-d603917b6f2d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Chris Evert, Mara Santangelo, Nathalie Dechy\n- Events: 1974 John Player Tournament, 2010 ASB Classic – Doubles\n- Roles: former professional tennis players, defending champions\n- Places: United States, Italy\n\nFacts:\n- Chris Evert was born on December 21, 1954, and she is a former World No. 1 professional tennis player from the United States.\n- Chris Evert was known as Chris Evert Lloyd from 1979 to 1987.\n- The first-seeded Chris Evert won the singles title at the 1974 John Player Tournament and earned £1,750 ($4,200) in first-prize money.\n- Mara Santangelo was born on 28 June 1981, and she is a former professional tennis player from Italy.\n- Nathalie Dechy and Mara Santangelo were the defending champions for the 2010 ASB Classic – Doubles.\n- Before the 2010 ASB Classic – Doubles, Nathalie Dechy retired from tennis and could not defend the title, and Mara Santangelo chose not to participate that year.",
